// Supabase backend config (TEMPLATE — committed, no real secret).
//
// The app reads the Supabase project URL and the PUBLIC publishable key at
// RUNTIME to talk to the backend. The publishable key is a PUBLIC client key —
// it is fine on the device. NEVER put the secret service-role key here (it
// bypasses row-level security); that key stays server-side only.
//
// SETUP (one time, per developer machine):
//   1. Copy this file to iosApp/Supabase.xcconfig (same folder, drop ".template"):
//        cp iosApp/Supabase.xcconfig.template iosApp/Supabase.xcconfig
//   2. Replace the PLACEHOLDER values below with your real project URL +
//      publishable key (Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API).
//   3. The real iosApp/Supabase.xcconfig is gitignored — never commit real keys.
//
// Configuration/Config.xcconfig #includes iosApp/Supabase.xcconfig and the
// values are surfaced into Info.plist as `SupabaseURL` and `SupabasePublishableKey`.
// iOSApp.swift reads them at launch and calls FeedBridge.configureSupabase(...).
//
// NOTE on the URL: xcconfig treats `//` as a comment, so a bare
// `https://...` value would be truncated at the `//`. We therefore store the
// URL WITHOUT the scheme (host only) and re-add `https://` in Swift. See
// SUPABASE_URL below.

// Host only (no scheme) to avoid the xcconfig `//` comment pitfall. Swift
// prepends "https://". e.g. abcdefghijkl.supabase.co
SUPABASE_URL = PLACEHOLDER.supabase.co
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY = PLACEHOLDER
